# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE MOST IMPORTANT FILE IN THIS REPO.
#
# This system ingests CVs, salary floors, family circumstances and, if you use
# it honestly, things you would not say out loud at work. None of that belongs
# in version control on a public host.
#
# Everything you or the agent generates is ignored by default. The repo tracks
# scaffolding only. If you WANT history for your own wiki, make it a separate
# private repo inside wiki/ rather than loosening these rules.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

sources/*
!sources/.gitkeep
!sources/README.md

wiki/*
!wiki/.gitkeep

# Radar working files: regenerated every run, and seen.json records what you
# have been shown, which is itself a record of your job search.
tools/radar/*.json
tools/radar/shortlist.md
config.json

# ...but the example config MUST ship, or a fresh clone cannot run the radar
# at all. README, radar.py and the role-radar skill all tell the user to copy
# it. Caught 2026-08-24 by checking what a clone would actually contain.
!tools/radar/config.example.json

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env

# Oversight layer: API keys
tools/review/config.json

# oversight/ -- the folder the user opens in another vendor's tool.
# The brief is tracked so it exists from clone time and is discoverable before
# any application is built. Everything generated beside it is a copy of the
# user's outgoing documents and is not.
oversight/*
!oversight/OVERSIGHT.md
